$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
9-(2',3',5'-tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-6-(4-chlorophenyl)thio-2-chloro-9H-purine
(8a) Potassium carbonate (91 mg, 0.66 mmol, 1.2 equiv.) was added to a
solution of 4-chlorothiophenol (94 mg, 0.65 mmol, 1.19 equiv.) in DMF (5
mL) and stirred for 15 min at room temperature. A solution of
9-(2',3',5'-tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-2,6-dichloropurine 3 (244 mg,
0.54 mmol, 1 equiv.) in DMF (5 mL) was added and the resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at 35°C for 1 h (HPLC Control). Then the reaction
mixture was diluted with EtOAc (40 mL) and the organic phase was washed
with brine (7×25 mL), dried over anh. Na2SO4 and evaporated under reduced
pressure. Silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc; gradient
33%→66%), Product 8a (297 mg, 98%) as a white foam. Rf = 0.48
(hexane/EtOAc = 1:2). IR (KBr): 2718, 1752, 1560, 1477, 1342, 1232, 1093;
1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 8.14 (s, 1H, H-C(8)), 7.56 (d, 2H, 3 J =
8.5 Hz, Ar), 7.43 (d, 2H, 3 J = 8.5 Hz, Ar), 6.19 (d, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' = 5.5
Hz, H-C(1')), 5.78 (t, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' = 3 J 2'-3' = 5.5 Hz, H-C(2')), 5.57
(dd, 1H, 3 J 2'-3' = 5.5 Hz, 3 J 3'-4' = 4.2 Hz, H-C(3')), 4.45 (dt, 1H,
3 J 3'-4' = 3 J 4'-5b' = 4.2 Hz, 3 J 4'-5a' = 3.2 Hz, H-C(4')), 4.42 (dd,
1H, 3 J 4'-5a' = 3.2 Hz, 2 J 5a'-5b' = 12.7 Hz, Ha-C(5')), 4.37 (dd, 1H,
3 J 4'-5b' = 4.2 Hz, 2 J 5a'-5b' = 12.7 Hz, Hb-C(5')), 2.15, 2.14, 2.08
(3s, 9H, H3COOC-C(2',3',5')); 13C-NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 170.2,
169.5, 169.3, 162.6, 154.0, 150.0, 141.4, 136.6, 136.2, 130.1, 129.5,
124.5, 86.1, 80.6, 73.2, 70.6, 62.9, 20.8, 20.5, 20.3; HRMS (ESI) calcd.
for C22H21N4O7Cl2S [M + H]+, 555.0503; found 555.0501.
